# Security headers for the static site.
# Netlify and Cloudflare Pages read this file automatically; for other hosts,
# copy these headers into the host's config (see "Security" in CLAUDE.md).
# `npm run preview` also serves them, so a local build behaves like production.
#
# The main Content-Security-Policy is added to index.html at build time
# (vite.config.js). frame-ancestors only works as a real header, so it is here.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
